  "id": "COMPOUND:16783 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "Flavipin is shown to have a target relationship with Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which in turn is targeted by Spathelia bischromene and [(1S,2R,4S,5R,8R,10S,13R,14R,17S,18R)-2-hydroxy-4,5,9,9,13,20,20-heptamethyl-24-oxahexacyclo[15.5.2.01,18.04,17.05,14.08,13]tetracosan-10-yl] acetate. This compound is also targeted by Flavipin, and it ultimately targets CCF-STTG1. The evidence suggests a chain of molecular interactions where Flavipin influences the activity of a compound that, in turn, modulates CCF-STTG1. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but the exact mechanism by which Flavipin affects CCF-STTG1 remains unclear. The evidence supports a potential role for Flavipin in modulating the activity of a downstream target, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance of this pathway.",
